.TH CTAGS 1 2026-10-21 quicktags
.SH NAME
ctags \- generate tags files for C, C++, and Fortran
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctags
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctags
writes a tags file indexing the definitions in C, C++, and Fortran
sources, for Vim and other editors to jump to them.
It is quicktags, a fast replacement for Universal Ctags 6.2.1, whose
options it takes and whose tags files it matches, except where those
are wrong.
.PP
Each
.I file
is tagged by its extension, and each directory is tagged recursively.
Files without an extension of a known language are skipped, and so are
version control directories and build products, such as
.B .git
and
.BR *.o .
With no
.I file
and
.BR \-R ,
the current directory is tagged.
Files are tagged in parallel, and the output does not depend on the
number of threads.
.PP
The tags file is written as
.BR tags ,
sorted, with a short header of pseudo-tags.
Each tag gives its name, its file, a search pattern for its line, and
fields: its kind, its line number, its enclosing scope, its type, and
whether it is visible only in its file.
The file is replaced at once when complete, so an editor never reads a
partial one, and a file that is not a tags file is never overwritten.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Input
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-recurse [ =yes | no ]
With no
.IR file ,
tag the current directory.
Directories are always tagged recursively.
.TP
.BI \-L " file"
Also tag the files named by
.IR file ,
one per line, or by standard input for
.BR \- .
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are skipped, and lines starting with
.B \-
are options.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude= pattern \fR|\fB@ file
Skip files and directories whose name or path matches the shell
.IR pattern ,
or any pattern listed in
.IR file .
An empty value clears the list, including the default exclusions.
.TP
.BI \-\-exclude\-exception= pattern \fR|\fB@ file
Tag matching names even though excluded.
.TP
.B \-\-links=no
Skip symbolic links to files.
Links to directories are always skipped.
.TP
.BI \-\-options= file
Read options from
.IR file ,
one per line, or from the
.B *.ctags
files in a directory.
.B NONE
does nothing: no option files are ever read implicitly.
.SS Languages
.TP
.BR \-\-languages= [ + | \- ] \fIlist\fR
Tag only the languages listed, of
.BR C ,
.BR C++ ,
and
.BR Fortran ,
or add or remove them.
.TP
.BI \-\-language\-force= language
Tag every file as
.IR language .
.TP
.BI \-\-langmap= language : map\fR[\fB,\fR.\|.\|.]
.TQ
.BR \-\-map\- \fIlanguage\fR=[ + | \- ] \fImap\fR
Choose the files of a language by extensions such as
.B .c.h
and patterns such as
.BR (*.x) ;
a leading
.B +
adds to the defaults.
For example,
.B \-\-langmap=c:+.h
tags
.B .h
files as C instead of C++.
.TP
.BR \-h " [" + "]\fIextensions\fR|" default
The extensions of header files, such as
.BR .h.hpp ,
whose tags are never file-scoped.
.TP
.BR \-\-kinds\- \fIlanguage\fR=[ + | \- ] \fIkinds\fR
Enable or disable kinds of tags, as letters or
.BI { name }\fR.
.B \-\-help
lists the kinds, and which are enabled by default.
For example,
.B \-\-kinds\-C=+p
adds prototypes.
The older
.BI \-\- language \-kinds=
is the same.
.TP
.BR \-I " \fIlist\fR|" @\fIfile\fR | \-
Identifiers for the C and C++ parser to ignore:
.I X
drops
.IR X ,
.IB X +
drops it and the parenthesized arguments after it, and
.IB X = Y
and
.IB X += Y
replace them with
.IR Y .
Useful for macros that confuse parsing, such as
.B __init
or
.BR EXPORT_SYMBOL+ .
.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-f " " \fIfile\fR ", " \-o " " \fIfile
Write to
.IR file ,
or to standard output for
.BR \- ,
without pseudo-tags.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-append [ =yes | no ]
Add to an existing tags file, replacing the tags of the files tagged
again.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-sort=yes | no | foldcase
Sort the tags, ignoring case with
.BR foldcase ,
or leave them in the order found, as
.B \-u
does.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-output\-format=etags
Write an Emacs
.B TAGS
file instead.
.TP
.B \-\-output\-format=e\-ctags
Write Exuberant Ctags' variant of the format.
.TP
.BR \-\-format=1 | 2
Format 1 writes no fields.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-N ", " \-\-excmd=number | pattern | mixed | combine
Address tags by line number, by search pattern, or by both.
The default, mixed, uses patterns except for Fortran common blocks.
.TP
.BI \-\-pattern\-length\-limit= n
Cut patterns at
.I n
bytes, or never for 0 (default 96).
.TP
.BR \-\-tag\-relative [ =yes | no | always | never ]
Name files relative to the directory of the tags file, or absolutely
for
.BR never .
.SS Extras and fields
.TP
.BR \-\-extras= [ + | \- ] \fIextras\fR
Enable or disable extra tags:
.B q
also tags C and C++ names qualified by their scope, such as
.BR ns::Class::f ,
for jumping to a member by its full name;
.B f
tags each file by its name;
.B F
includes tags visible only in their file;
.B p
writes the pseudo-tags.
.B F
and
.B p
are enabled by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-fields= [ + | \- ] \fIfields\fR
Choose the fields written, as letters or
.BI { name }\fR.
The default is
.BR fknst :
the file scope, kind, line, scope, and type.
.B +iaS
adds base classes, access, and signatures, as completion plugins use.
.B \-\-list\-fields
lists them all.
.SS Other
.TP
.BR \-\-list\-languages ", " \-\-list\-kinds [ =\fIlanguage\fR] ", " \-\-list\-kinds\-full [ =\fIlanguage\fR] ", " \-\-list\-extras ", " \-\-list\-fields
List these as Universal Ctags does.
.TP
.BI \-\-jobs= n
Use
.I n
threads, or one per processor for 0, the default.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the options and the kinds.
.PP
Universal Ctags' other options are accepted where they would change
nothing here, as are options naming its other languages.
Those that would change the tags, such as
.B \-\-regex\-C
or
.BR \-D ,
are refused.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B tags
The default output.
.TP
.B TAGS
The default output with
.BR \-e .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, including when some inputs could not be read, 1 on an
error, and 2 when out of memory.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
ctags \-R
ctags \-\-kinds\-C=+p \-f tags.local src
ctags \-R \-\-extras=+q \-\-fields=+iaS \-\-exclude=build
ctags \-a src/main.c
git ls\-files | ctags \-L \-
ctags \-e \-R
.fi
.SH NOTES
Each tag also carries a
.B line:
field, which Universal Ctags writes only with
.BR \-\-fields=+n ,
so that an editor starts its search at the tag's line.
Lines end with a line feed, also on Windows.
.PP
Files larger than 64 MiB are skipped with a warning, and blocks and
Fortran units nested more than 1024 deep are read as part of the
construct around them.
.PP
Where the output departs from Universal Ctags, and why, is described in
.B docs/spec.md
in the source.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vim (1)
